\par\par \b \uc2  Asia-Pacific Central Bk -2: Different Views On  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 397 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juli 1997\par 09:47\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  'There was the usual rhetoric about speculators,' the official said. 'But the point was made a world full of mobile capital is a difficult and dangerous world for central banks that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .' \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials argued against \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in all cases - arguing that its experience of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets showed that the best policy is to let the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  find a bottom and only then give it a boost when it's already headed higher. \par \par \uc2  An official in the Bank of Japan's international department confirmed that is the BOJ attitude - based on its past experience, it's better to let the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  find a bottom or a ceiling rather than try to pinpoint a certain level via \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said. \par \par \uc2  Despite heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem speculative pressures, Thailand, the Philippines and Malaysia have all been forced this month to abandon efforts to support their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  If created, the EMEAP fund would likely be of greatest immediate interest to Thailand and the Philippines, both struggling with the aftermath of the decisions to float their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Thailand announced this week it will seek help from the IMF to right its economy after the plunge of the baht. The Philippines has already stepped up its borrowings from the IMF to rebuild reserves that were depleted in defending the peso. \par \par \uc2  But such an EMEAP fund would likely come with strings attached, according to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official. \par \par \uc2  Japan in particular insisted at the meeting that any EMEAP money wouldn't be used to fight \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators. It would only be used to further IMF-inspired economic adjustments - though that was loosely defined at the meeting, according to the official. \par \par \uc2  The money, which would likely go into reserve accounts at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , could be used to fund a budget deficit or provide funds for the banking sector. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Japan governor Yasuo Matsushita led the Japanese delegation. After the meeting, BOJ executive director Takashi Anzai told reporters that EMEAP had only agreed to 'study' the issue of extra funding for countries in difficulty. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official who attended the meeting said there was a 'reasonably strong presumption' among Southeast Asian central banks that some kind of EMEAP loan fund would emerge. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 29-07-97 \par \par \uc2  0747GMT \par \par \uc2  1134 4204 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7t05dzo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
