\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand, Japan to cooperate on  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2 --MOF. \b0\par\par\uc2 364 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juli 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 18 (Reuter) - Thailand and Japan have agreed to cooperate to promote stability in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, and cooperative measures could include \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a senior official from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The official briefed reporters following a meeting between Thai Finance Minister Thanong Bidaya and Japanese Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka. \par \par \uc2  The meeting was also attended by Bank of Thailand Governor Rerngchai Marakanond, he said. \par \par \uc2  "Finance Minister Mitsuzuka and Thai Finance Minister Thanong agreed that we will cooperate closely in the markets for a stable baht. This includes \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the baht," the official said. \par \par \uc2  Asked if any concrete measures for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  cooperation, such as the use of a repo pact, were discussed during the meeting, the official declined to comment. \par \par \uc2  "There was no request from the Thai side for financial support," he added. \par \par \uc2  Thailand was not asking for any financial support from the International Monetary Fund (IMF) or the Export-Import Bank of Japan, the official said. \par \par \uc2  "Thailand is asking for technical assistance from the IMF, as it had been before. It is not asking for financial support from the IMF," the official said. \par \par \uc2  There were no discussions about support from Japanese banks, either, he added. \par \par \uc2  Asked whether the Thais called on Japan to join an international support scheme in the future should a need arise for one, the official said the issue was not discussed. \par \par \uc2  Most of the 40-minute talk was dominated by Thailand explaining its move towards a managed floating system for the baht and financial and fiscal steps taken for the economy, the official said. \par \par \uc2  Both the Thai finance minister and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said those measures will help Thai economic growth, he said. \par \par \uc2  Mitsuzuka was quoted as telling the Thai officials that the steps taken were timely and appropriate. MOF minister also told them that he believed that the Thai authorities will be successful in bringing the matter under control, he said. \par \par \uc2  Asked whether Thailand explained about their foreign reserves, the official said the topic was not discussed. \par \par \uc2  Thailand did not explain to the Japanese side their economic outlook, he added. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7i02h2w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
