\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Agrees To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  To Support Thai Baht If Warranted \b0\par\par\uc2 282 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juli 1997\par 13:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones Online News \par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  promised to work closely with Thai monetary authorities to help stabilize the baht and pledged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on behalf of the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if necessary, a \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said Friday. \par \par \uc2  The official, briefing reporters on the meeting between Thai Finance Minister Thanong Bidaya and his Japanese counterpart, Hiroshi Mitsuzuka, said Thanong didn't request any financial support from Japan during the meeting. \par \par \uc2  Thanong told his Japanese counterparts that Thailand hasn't requested such aid from the International Monetary Fund, the official said. \par \par \uc2  He said the two men spent the better part of their meeting discussing recent developments in Thailand's economy and financial markets and that Mitsuzuka assured his counterpart that the Bank of Thailand's decision July 2 to conduct a managed float of the baht was the "proper" one. \par \par \uc2  "I believe Thailand's efforts will be successful," Mitsuzuka was quoted saying. \par \par \uc2  The official declined to say if specific methods of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were discussed at the meeting, which was attended by Bank of Thailand Governor Rerngchai Marakanond and other Thai officials. From the Japan side, Eisuke Sakakibara, vice minister of international affairs, also attended. \par \par \uc2  The Thai delegation met with various economic officials and representatives from the banking and business worlds during their visit to Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The finance ministry official said that Thai officials didn't request any financial support from private Japanese banks during their stay. \par \par \uc2  Regarding Thailand's economy, the official noted that Thailand has suffered a "mini-bubble" during the last three years or so. \par \par \uc2  Copyright (c) 1997 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Dokument djon000020011006dt7i00grw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
