\par\par \b \uc2  BIS Annual Report:  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Reserves Rose Sharply In 96 \b0\par\par\uc2 283 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 1997\par 11:33\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BASEL (AP-Dow Jones)--International \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves grew by a record $196.5 billion in 1996 despite the fact that German and U.S. monetary authorities didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in the period, the Bank for International Settlements said in its annual report Monday. \par \par \uc2  Most of the growth in official reserves took place in Asia, notably China, and in Latin America. In Europe, Italy and Spain built up reserves on \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars and Deutsche marks, the report said. \par \par \uc2  Exchange-rate-adjusted dollar reserves grew $145.8 billion in 1996. In 1995, total \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves grew $181.8 billion, while dollar reserves increased $156.1 billion. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. financed most of its current account deficit in 1996 with official inflows, the BIS said. A stronger dollar and 'a pervasive search for yield in world financial markets' led to strong capital flows to emerging markets. 'Since many of these countries link their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the dollar, the resulting \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  led to increases in reserves,' the report said. These were generally invested in U.S. Treasurys and other liquid dollar instruments. \par \par \uc2  In Japan, the $14 billion increase in reserves over the last nine months of 1996 'appears to represent mainly the flow of earnings on stock of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves that reached $207 billion by the end of the year,' the BIS said. In the first quarter of 1996, Japanese reserves grew $21 billion on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and interest receipts. In the following twelve months, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't seem to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the report said. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 09-06-97 \par \par \uc2  0933GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt69047or\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
