\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 :Dollar Rises On Japan Comments, SNB Statement \b0\par\par\uc2  By John Carreyrou \par \uc2 299 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Mai 1997\par 22:22\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK (AP-Dow Jones)--The dollar gained against most major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday, after Japanese officials reiterated that the yen has risen too far too fast, and the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  squashed the franc's recent rally. \par \par \uc2  The dollar recouped much of the ground it lost Tuesday against the Deutsche mark and the yen after the U.S. Federal Reserve left key interest rates unchanged. \par \par \uc2  The dollar initially rose in Asia when Japan's finance minister and another influential monetary official expressed concern for the second time in two days about the yen's abrupt appreciation. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka told Parliament an 'excessively strong' yen was undesirable, and hinted that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop its rise. \par \par \uc2  At the same parliament session, Eisuke Sakakibara, who heads the ministry's international finance bureau, echoed Mitsuzuka's comments, calling for stable exchange rates. \par \par \uc2  'The comments from Mitsuzuka and Sakakibara got the dollar going,' encouraging traders who were short dollars to book profits from Tuesday's drop, said Lisa Finstrom, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Smith Barney in New York. \par \par \uc2  In Europe, the dollar got a second boost when the Swiss National Bank (SNB) announced it had pumped liquidity into money markets to soften the Swiss franc. Traders promptly sold Swiss francs for dollars and marks. Traders have been buying Swiss francs heavily on concern that Europe's future single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be weak. \par \par \uc2  Late in New York, the dollar was quoted at DM1.6930, up from DM1.6750 late Tuesday in New York. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also quoted at Y114.35, up from Y112.55. Sterling was trading at $1.6450, down from $1.6570. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 21-05-97 \par \par \uc2  2022GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 1865 4164 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5l03pwc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
