\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ says may  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  to help support Thai baht. \b0\par\par\uc2 322 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, May 15 (Reuter) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in financial markets to help support the Thai baht if asked to do so by Thailand as part of the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  safety net agreement reached in 1996, a BOJ official said. \par \par \uc2  "The agreement is there, although it is not a thing we would activate unless we were asked by Thailand," the official told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  Last year, Japan agreed with the monetary authorities of Australia, Hong Kong, Indonesia, Malaysia, the Philippines, Singapore and Thailand to establish bilateral repurchase agreements to provide liquidity in times of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis. \par \par \uc2  Such "repo" pacts give participants instant access to cash -- for use to defend their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against excessive volatility -- by virtue of them selling their holdings in U.S. government securities to partners with a promise to buy them back later. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, in the first use of this agreement, the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to defend the baht. \par \par \uc2  Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  were also said to have bought the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after it fell to 26.250-26.300 to the dollar, though there was no confirmation. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ official said: "We have an agreement, and if we want to use it, we certainly will. \par \par \uc2  "But it's not a question of our making the first move," he added. \par \par \uc2  He declined to comment on whether preparations for such a move are currently in progress. \par \par \uc2  Earlier in the day, Thai Finance Minister Amnuay Viravan said Thailand will defend its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against attacks in the market by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators. \par \par \uc2  "We have support from all our friends," he told reporters at a symposium in Tokyo on Asia's future. \par \par \uc2  The baht was up by late Tokyo trade, standing near 25.500-25.600 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt5f05n50\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
