\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  MOF Official -2: No Comment On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Report \b0\par\par\uc2 181 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 1997\par 11:25\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (AP-Dow Jones)--A senior official at \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Wednesday that the ministry's position that recent movements in the global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets have been excessive remains unchanged. \par \par \uc2  The official, who spoke with Dow Jones on condition of anonymity, declined to discuss specific \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels, but noted that finance ministers from the Group of Seven leading industrialized nations (G-7) had reconfirmed their commitment to take cooperative action in the markets 'as needed.' \par \par \uc2  The official said he hadn't seen a report from Kyodo News Agency quoting an 'international monetary source' as saying the U.S., \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Germany had been preparing since Tuesday to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets, selling dollars and buying yen. \par \par \uc2  'Our policy remains unchanged that we don't discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' for the record, the official said. \par \par \uc2  Privately, some finance ministry officials have said during the last week that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could occur 'at any time' and investors buying dollars around current levels 'will get hurt.' \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 07-05-97 \par \par \uc2  0925GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt57033zc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
