\par\par \b \uc2  Hard to procure  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  funds from mkt--MOF. \b0\par\par\uc2 371 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, May 7 (Reuter) - Eisuke Sakakibara, director-general of the International Finance Bureau of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF), said on Wednesday it would be difficult to procure funds for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly from the money market. \par \par \uc2  Currently, most of the funds for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  are procured through the issuing of special \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  bills, called financing bills (FBs), that have been mostly underwritten by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ). \par \par \uc2  "If (the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) procures \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds from the money market, that would send a signal that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is on its way," Sakakibara said. \par \par \uc2  FBs usually carry interest rates that are lower than prevailing market rates and are not always in great demand in the market, and the BOJ is obligated to buy most of the issues that are left unsold in the market. \par \par \uc2  For decades, the BOJ has been proposing that the 60-day government paper should be designed for sale in the market, instead of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying most of the issue amount. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ argues that if FBs were saleable in the market, this would undoubtedly add to money market liquidity and the globalisation of the Tokyo financial market. \par \par \uc2  But Sakakibara said: "It's common among other nations that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds are raised via central banks and the treasury account... Thus it would be extremely difficult to raise funds from the market." \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara was speaking at a parliamentary finance committee meeting. \par \par \uc2  Helped by easy access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fund, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has in the past spent massively to exert influence on dollar/yen exchange rates. \par \par \uc2  Senior BOJ officials have said history shows that government financial dependence on a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that can print money without any limitations has caused hyperinflation that has ultimately ruined nations. \par \par \uc2  The FB rate is now at 0.375 percent or 0.125 percentage point below the discount rate, which currently stands at a record low 0.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  The outstanding volume of FBs totalled 29.835 trillion yen at the end of April. \par \par \uc2  The MOF and the Bank of Japan have been meeting since March to discuss the money market, including the contentious issue of FB underwriting by the BOJ. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt5705zwl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
