\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -3: Thursday Could Be Volatile, Traders Warn \b0\par\par\uc2 281 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 1997\par 23:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Traders warned that Thursday could be a volatile session for the dollar because most of Europe will be on holiday for May Day and Japan continues to be unofficially on vacation for Golden Week. \par \par \uc2  'You could see either a big move - exacerbated by low liquidity - or very quiet, range-bound trading. Either extreme is possible,' said Jack Griffin, vice president and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Fuji Bank in New York. \par \par \uc2  Comments made by Japanese officials late Tuesday and early Wedensday reinforced traders' concerns that a concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the U.S. and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is possible if the dollar rises too fast against the yen. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka said it would 'take a while' for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to absorb Sunday's G-7 statement and the U.S. and Japan were 'completely unified' on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. \par \par \uc2  Toyoo Gyohten, a former \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official who now heads Japan's Institute of International Finance, said he considers Sunday's G-7 statement to be too 'weak' to support the yen. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin, for his part, repeated his usual refrain at a speaking engagement in New York late Tuesday. He said the U.S.'s strong-dollar policy remained unchanged but he shared Japan's concerns over a weakening yen. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Deputy Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers was equally coy on Wednesday. Asked at which point a strengthening dollar becomes counterproductive for the economy, he said, 'that's a good try' and referred questioners about the dollar to Rubin and to Sunday's G-7 statement. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 30-04-97 \par \par \uc2  2131GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 1865 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt4u0397p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
