\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup: Dlr Mixed; Marginally Higher Vs Yen \b0\par\par\uc2  By Margaret M. Boitano \par \uc2 318 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 1997\par 07:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (AP-Dow Jones)--Interbank players and options dealers locked horns Wednesday in a choppy trading session that saw the dollar bounce around in a narrow range. \par \par \uc2  Short-term speculators tried to drive the dollar above the Y127.30 level, where a knock-out option was said to expire. But the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  encounterd difficulty breaching key resistance at Y127, where it met with a wall of options-related dollar selling. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is mixed Wednesday compared with its levels in New York late Tuesday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders said lingering fears that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  might conduct a yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the dollar's rapid rise is also putting downward pressure on the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Overnight remarks by former \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official Toyoo Gyohten that the most recent foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  statement issued by the Group of Seven nations earlier this week was too 'weak' to support the yen added fuel to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  jitters, traders said. \par \par \uc2  'The dollar will stay range-bound for a while,' said Hirokazu Note, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Sumitomo Bank. 'Whenever the dollar rises, so too will fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but there are still a lot of players, such as trust banks and oil companies, that have to buy dollars.' \par \par \uc2  Around 0530 GMT (1:30 a.m. EDT), the dollar is quoted at Y126.95, above Y126.93 late Tuesday in New York and up from Y126.83 late Tuesday in London. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also is at DM1.7232, lower than DM1.7263 late Tuesday in New York and below DM1.7244 in London Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The mark is quoted at Y73.67, up from Y73.53 in New York late Tuesday and above Y73.55 in London late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 30-04-97 \par \par \uc2  0537GMT \par \par \uc2  1034 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt4u033rj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
