\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo/Dlr Surges -3: Fears Over BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 272 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 April 1997\par 01:28\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Sterling is at $1.6245, unchanged from $1.6245 in New York late Friday, but above $1.6230 in Tokyo late Friday. \par \par \uc2  Traders cautioned that if the dollar plows through resistance at Y127 Monday, there is a possibility that their buying will be met with actual yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ). \par \par \uc2  'Market players will encounter selling interest at Y127 and it will take some time to digest those sales orders,' the Dutch bank trader said. \par \par \uc2  'Gradually the market will test the upside, but there is a possibility of the BOJ interevening (if the dollar moves significantly above Y127,' he added. \par \par \uc2  Though no specific \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels were mentioned in the G-7 statement, Japanese Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka has repeatedly said the yen's recent weakening against the dollar is 'excessive' and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  will take measures at the appropriate time. \par \par \uc2  After the G-7 communique was released, U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin reiterated that he shares Japan's concern over the recent yen moves. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is expected to trade between Y126.50-Y127.30 and DM1.7250-DM1.73780 in choppy Asian trading Monday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar also gained sharply against the mark early Monday. Traders said the sharp appreciation in the dollar against the yen also brought the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher against its German counterpart. \par \par \uc2  Remarks by Deutsche Bundesbank President Hans Tietmeyer that current \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates 'more or less' appropriately reflect economic fundamentals also gave the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  a lift. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 27-04-97 \par \par \uc2  2328GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt4r030ml\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
