\par\par \b \uc2  Japan Amb./Leaders/ \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -2:  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  'Natural' For Ministers \b0\par\par\uc2 330 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 April 1997\par 00:16\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Saito added that it would be 'a natural thing' for the U.S. and Japanese finance ministers to discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  when they meet on April 27 as part of the Group of Seven (G-7) nations in Washington. \par \par \uc2  Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin is hosting the regular Spring event, which brings together the finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chiefs from the U.S., Japan, Germany, France, the U.K., Italy and Canada. \par \par \uc2  U.K. Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke isn't expected to attend the event because of May 1 national elections in the U.K. But the dollar's status against the yen and various European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is sure to be reviewed on the weekend. \par \par \uc2  And \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders are wondering whether Clinton and Hashimoto will strike some sort of deal over \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid signs that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the U.S. are concerned about a further weakening of the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Saito didn't touch on these matters. But he said, that 'we don't think there are bilateral issues to have to be discussed on leaders' level. Obviously, we have issues, problems, to have to discuss and to negotiate, and we have been doing so.' \par \par \uc2  'We believe that we don't have any bilateral issues to have to be discussed or negotiated on the leaders level. Probably the prime minister will wish to explain his economic policy,' Saito said. \par \par \uc2  Rubin has underscored that Japan must move aggressively and quickly on economic deregulation to help offset a rising Japanese trade surplus. \par \par \uc2  'He is now carrying out - trying to carry out - very bold reforms and deregulation in Japan, and we expect that these reforms and deregulation...will serve to stimulate our economy,' Saito said, adding that 'the prime minister will wish to explain the thought behind such policies and will ask for understanding on the part of the United States government.' \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 22-04-97 \par \par \uc2  2216GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt4m0317k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
