\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo: Dlr Narrowly Mixed; Down Vs Yen On Rubin Talk \b0\par\par\uc2 395 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 April 1997\par 02:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (AP-Dow Jones)--The dollar is narrowly mixed in early Tokyo trading Tuesday compared with its levels late in New York Monday, lower against the yen as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders digest U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin's first hint that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be used to cap the dollar's rapid gains against the yen. \par \par \uc2  At an overnight press briefing in Washington, Rubin said that while there haven't been any changes in the U.S.'s \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, the Treasury 'will act when it's appropriate and not act when it's not appropriate' regarding its policy on the yen. Rubin also reiterated that he shares Japanese policymakers' concerns over the dollar's rise against the yen. \par \par \uc2  'One thing that is quite clear now is that the U.S. is trying to cooperate with Japanese policy makers,' said Yasuhisa Morikuni, treasury manager at Bank of America in Tokyo. 'The market has a certain kind of nervousness because officials (from both \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the U.S.) keep making statements on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' he said. \par \par \uc2  Immediately following the remarks, the dollar dipped to Y126.46 in New York. It has since edged even lower, touching an intraday low of Y126.39 at 0008 GMT (8:08 p.m. EDT). \par \par \uc2  Market players said the Rubin's latest remarks, coming on the heels of a chorus of comments last week by Japanese policymakers from \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is weighing on the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But widespread notions that an outright \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the U.S. isn't likely in light of the fragile state of the U.S. asset markets and ahead of key international meetings later this month suggests that the dollar isn't in for a strong correction, they added. \par \par \uc2  Around 0025 GMT (8:25 p.m. EDT Monday), the dollar is trading at Y126.48, down from Y126.57 around 0001 GMT (8:01 p.m. EDT) and below Y126.61 in New York late Monday. The dollar was quoted at Y126.31 late in Tokyo Monday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also trading at DM1.7320, higher than DM1.7317 earlier and above DM1.7310 late Monday in New York. The dollar was at DM1.7203 in Tokyo late Monday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 15-04-97 \par \par \uc2  0034GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt4f02oxe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
