\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar calms by late Tokyo after windy session. \b0\par\par\uc2 449 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, April 11 (Reuter) - The dollar calmed down by late Tokyo trading on Friday after a windy early session led by inconsistent statements made by government officials. \par \par \uc2  "An artificial attempt to check a further slide by the yen may not yield any result, given that Japan's low interest rates are pushing Japanese capital abroad," said Kabun Muto, director-general of the Management and Coordination Agency. \par \par \uc2  Muto's remark drove the dollar up to a high of 126.25 yen. \par \par \uc2  Most traders expect dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) if the dollar surges to near 127 yen again. \par \par \uc2  Muto added that there was nothing wrong with the dollar moving above 125 yen, adding that in terms of purchasing-power parity, 150 yen to the dollar would be appropriate. \par \par \uc2  But those dollar gains were soon pared after a \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official told Reuters: "Muto's remarks regarding the dollar/yen rate do not reflect the official policy of the Japanese government." \par \par \uc2  "The official view is, as the Finance Minister (Hiroshi Mitsuzuka) said, that the yen's recent falls are overdone and (the ministry) is concerned about it," the MOF official added. \par \par \uc2  On credit policy, Muto also said the Bank of Japan should increase its official discount rate (ODR) by the end of this year to discourage capital outflows from Japan, he said. \par \par \uc2  Muto's remark on credit policy also pushed up the yields of Japanese government bonds (JGBs). \par \par \uc2  But the rise in the JGB yields failed to strengthen the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to lingering dollar-buying interest by institutional investors and local importers, traders said. \par \par \uc2  BOJ Governor Yasuo Matsushita said on Friday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not conduct monetary policy on the basis of foreign interest rates and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements alone. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders said that the only means currently available to check a further slide in the yen would be dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a credit tightening does not appear to be on the cards for the BOJ. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is set for an imminent action (dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), but they will have to do it alone," said Takeshi Hanai, executive manager of Industrial Bank of Japan Ltd's International Treasury Department. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin said that he shared Japan's concern about the yen's recent fall, but also reiterated that the strong dollar is in the U.S. interest. \par \par \uc2  Traders said Rubin's remark implied the Treasury supports BOJ's bid to check a dollar rally, but was reluctant to use its own money. \par \par \uc2  -- Yoshiko Mori, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8676 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt4b076b0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
