\par\par \b \uc2  G-7 Watch/Japan MOF -2: Jawboning Won't Reverse Uptrend \b0\par\par\uc2 320 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 1997\par 12:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Since a week ago, the dollar has risen by more than four yen, touching new highs not seen since August 1992. Earlier Thursday, the dollar soared to a new 55-month high of Y127.14. \par \par \uc2  Though the rapid pace at which the dollar is gaining ground against the yen has raised fears of a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , most traders said that anything short of a coordinated move by the Group of Seven (G-7) industrialized nations won't succeed in stemming the dollar's uptrend. \par \par \uc2  'This \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is still reflecting fundamentals,' said Makoto Kojima, chief corporate dealer at Barclays Bank in Tokyo. 'If you look at interest rate differentials, Japan's fragile financial sector... the dollar/yen should go up; it's a natural movement,' he added. \par \par \uc2  Kojima said that in coming weeks market will try to push the dollar to the Y128 level while a target of Y130 could be reached by mid-May. \par \par \uc2  Underpinning the trend for a higher dollar is strong dollar-demand by Japanese institutional investors, who continue to move funds to higher-yeilding foreign assets. \par \par \uc2  No amount of jawboning by the MOF is likely to reverse this tide, analysts said, noting that prospects for raising Japan's historically-low interest rates are dim. \par \par \uc2  Meantime, the market isn't convinced that the U.S. would support a concerted move to push down the dollar. \par \par \uc2  'In terms of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , if \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  made a move now, I don't think it would be in agreement with the U.S. Treasury Department,' said Kenneth Landan, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Morgan Grenfell in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin's main concern is the U.S. bond market and any 'hint' of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would result in a 'sharp decline in bond prices,' he said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 10-04-97 \par \par \uc2  1056GMT \par \par \uc2  1134 4201 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt4a02jv2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
