\par\par \b \uc2  U.S. Rubin: Didn't Discuss  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2  With  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 287 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 1997\par 07:15\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  YOKOTA AIR FORCE BASE, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (AP-Dow Jones)--U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin says \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  generally and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  specifically weren't discussed in his recent meetings with Japanese officials. \par \par \uc2  Rubin, speaking to reporters traveling with him back to the U.S. after a three-nation Asia tour, said the 'primary goal' of his April 4 visit to Tokyo was to 'have a discussion with the prime minister and the finance minister with respect to the Japanese economy and its prospects.' \par \par \uc2  The secretary underscored during those visits the need for Japan to move forcefully ahead with economic deregulation, although he raised some questions over the pace of liberalization and whether it would be enough to offset fiscal drag caused by various tax measures that took effect April 1. \par \par \uc2  If not, Rubin suggest markets might be a disciplining force on the Japanese economy, although he has reiterated numerous times in recent days that his comments shouldn't be viewed as offering any direction about which way the dollar should go, nor that \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be a tool of trade policy. \par \par \uc2  The Treasury secretary, questioned Tuesday during a brief refueling stop at this U.S. air base outside Tokyo about statements in recent days by Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  which suggested authorities may be hoping to cap further dollar gains, replied: 'They haven't discussed it with us.' \par \par \uc2  'We never discussed exchange rates at all' at either the Tokyo meetings, nor at the Asia Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) meeting in the Philippines on April 5-6, Rubin added. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka attended the APEC event. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 09-04-97 \par \par \uc2  0515GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt4902fwp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
