\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : -2:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fears Chill Dollar \b0\par\par\uc2 347 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 April 1997\par 23:15\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Early on Tuesday, an unnamed Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  official was rumored to be threatening \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Y126.50. That, coupled with a rumor out of Germany that the Bundesbank was selling 10-year Bunds to raise dollars for an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  action, 'spooked people out of long dollar positions,' said Richard Vullo, vice-president of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Bayerische Hypotheken-und Wechsel Bank AG in New York. \par \par \uc2  The move out of dollars was quickly reversed, however. As the belief becomes more pervasive that the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will appear on time and Japanese investors return in force to offshore markets in pursuit of higher interest rates, traders now see only one direction for the dollar - up. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's latest upward move, which began Friday in New York, is now being driven mostly by players in Europe, some traders noted. \par \par \uc2  The European tinge to the rally has led some to believe that the debate over the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the driving factor. German Finance Minister Theo Waigel was reported on Monday to have said he would take a more relaxed stance toward the interpretation of the Maastricht treaty's deficit criteria. Hence, a majority in the market now believes European Monetary Union will proceed in time. That depresses the mark, thus helping the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Sakamoto at National Australia Bank said the dollar would 'go up and down like a yo-yo' against the mark in line with the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate , and that it didn't matter on which continent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves were being initiated. \par \par \uc2  'We're all looking at exactly the same things,' Sakamoto said. If traders made two steps forward in Europe, for example, that would be followed by one step forward in New York. Two steps backward in New York would be followed by one step back in Asia, he said. \par \par \uc2  Sakamoto said the dollar continues to be attractive simply because U.S. interest rates are higher than in Japan and Germany. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 08-04-97 \par \par \uc2  2115GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 1865 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt4802eft\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
