\par\par \b \uc2  Fed, BOJ won't  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  mart soon - US experts. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Roanne Daniels \par \uc2 659 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 April 1997\par 20:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, April 7 (Reuter) - U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  experts said chances were slim to none that the Federal Reserve or Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the dollar's rise despite a 50-month peak against the yen on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Central banks were unlikely to get involved unless the dollar's ascent quickens, it breaks above the critical 130-yen barrier, or U.S. officials temper their strong-dollar rhetoric, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders and analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "At this point, there's absolutely no chance of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The strong dollar is the best thing that has happened to Japan," said John Praveen, senior international economist at Merrill Lynch and Co Inc. \par \par \uc2  He spoke shortly after the dollar peaked at 125.81 yen, its highest level since January 1993. \par \par \uc2  Chris Iggo, international economist at BZW Securities Inc in New York, said last week's release of the BoJ's "tankan" survey of business sentiment showed a soft economy and pessimistic corporate outlook for the near-term. \par \par \uc2  "The only bright spot really is the export sector and a weaker yen will help exports even more," Iggo said. \par \par \uc2  "For the BoJ to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be a bit of a policy mistake," he added. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said any effort by U.S. monetary authorities to rein in the greenback would blatantly contradict the strong-dollar policy oft-stated by Treasury officials and fly in the face of Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin's remarks last week before a highly publicized trip to Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  "It would be very counter-productive for the U.S. to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when their current stance is for a strong dollar. That would seem very contradictory to me," said Tom Arnold, chief dealer at Dai-Ichi Kangyo Bank in New York. \par \par \uc2  "Most people don't see any possibility of Federal Reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he added. \par \par \uc2  Rubin urged \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to guard against a resurgence of its trade surplus but stressed that using \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates to manipulate trade accounts was not the best method. \par \par \uc2  "If the U.S. was involved in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  now, it would go against everything Rubin has said," Iggo said. \par \par \uc2  The Dow Jones industrials index had gained over 45 points and the 30-year long bond had added nearly half a point by mid-afternoon. \par \par \uc2  "The only damage the dollar seems to be doing is to the U.S.-Japan trade balance and I think the focus is more on inflation than trade, so I would say the odds are pretty low for concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he added. \par \par \uc2  The dollar jumped on Monday despite news of a rise in Japan's current account surplus for the second month in a row. Before January, the trade surplus had shrunk for 17 months. \par \par \uc2  Traders said Rubin in effect "took the dollar off the table" when it came to trade negotiations between nations, thus allowing the greenback greater freedom on the upside and, in part, sparking Monday's rally. \par \par \uc2  U.S. asset markets reacted positively to the dollar's strength as overseas investors rushed to capitalize on the move and bought Treasuries and stocks, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "It seems to me with both U.S. stocks and bonds rallying that none of the Group of Seven have a real keen interest in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Mike Malpede, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Refco Group Ltd in Chicago. \par \par \uc2  The February surplus rose 15.4 percent to 865.2 billion yen ($6.92 billion) from a year earlier. \par \par \uc2  Dealers also spoke of past failures of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the face of strong economic disparities between nations and of the current inability of nations to alter fiscal policy to manipulate exchange rates. \par \par \uc2  "There's not much they can do but talk down the dollar. The prospect of the U.S. lowering rates and Japan raising rates is not on the agenda," Merrill's Praveen said. \par \par \uc2  (( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1677 )) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt4707ow1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
