\par\par \b \uc2  Japan MOF/BOJ to meet to discuss money market, FBs. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Yoshiko Mori \par \uc2 612 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 3 (Reuter) - Japan's powerful monetary authorities, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) and the Bank of Japan (BOJ), will meet as early as later this month to discuss issues in the money market, including short-term debt underwriting by the BOJ, a MOF official said on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "The subjects of the meeting include the sales method for Financing Bills (FBs), the legal status of money brokers and the Real Time Gross Settlement system," the MOF official told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  It has not yet been decided how often they will meet, he added. \par \par \uc2  Depending on the outcome of the meeting, it may point to a change in Japan's approach of influencing \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates via quantitative \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  For decades, the BOJ has been proposing that 60-day government paper, called FBs, should be sold in the market, instead of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying most of the issue amount. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ argues that if FBs are designed for sale in the market, this would undoubtedly add to money market liquidity and the globalisation of the Tokyo financial market. \par \par \uc2  However, the MOF official said that the FBs should not be discussed only from the money-market perspective. \par \par \uc2  MOF raises yen for market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the issuance of FBs, which carry interest rates that are lower than prevailing market rates. \par \par \uc2  Due to the low yield, FBs are not always in great demand and the BOJ is obligated to buy most of the issues that are left unsold. \par \par \uc2  The FB rate is now at 0.375 percent or 0.125 percentage point below the discount rate, currently standing at a record low. \par \par \uc2  The outstanding volume of FBs totalled 25.20 trillion yen at the end of February. \par \par \uc2  Another MOF official said that if FB rates are set in line with the market, it would mean a heavier fiscal burden that may not be acceptable to taxpayers. \par \par \uc2  Helped by easy access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fund, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent an estimated $64.73 billion to rein in the galloping yen in the two years to December 1996. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ has made no secret of its discontent over MOF's reliance on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to finance \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  A BOJ spokesman said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current stance has been reflected in recent remarks by its governor. \par \par \uc2  BOJ Governor Yasuo Matsushita said last month that the question of whether FBs are an appropriate way of raising funds for \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  requires some consideration. \par \par \uc2  The question of FBs being underwritten by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not an issue to be looked at only in the context of the BOJ law, and provisions in the Budget law should also be taken into account, Matsushita said. \par \par \uc2  An article in the Budget law bars the BOJ from underwriting government long-term debt. \par \par \uc2  Under a proposed revision to the BOJ law, the BOJ would still be able to buy FBs. \par \par \uc2  But, despite the fact that FBs are a form of short-term debt, they are constantly rolled over, making the BOJ's FB purchases "de facto" underwriting of long-term government debt. \par \par \uc2  France and Germany have banned government underwriting of both short- and long-term debt as part of their moves toward European economic and monetary union and a European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In the United States, debt underwriting by the Federal Reserve has long been prohibited. \par \par \uc2  Senior BOJ officials said that history shows that government financial dependence on a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that can print money without any limitations has caused hyperinflation that has ultimately ruined nations. \par \par \uc2  ---Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8676 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt330949d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
