\par\par \b \uc2  Tokyo Midday/Dlr Plunges -2: Dlr Drops Vs HK$ \b0\par\par\uc2 321 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 1997\par 02:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The mark is at Y73.19, down from Y73.30 earlier in Tokyo and below Y73.29 in New York late Wednesday. The mark was quoted in Tokyo late Wednesday at 73.54 yen. \par \par \uc2  Sterling is at $1.6170, down from $1.6195 earlier in Tokyo and below $1.6153 in New York late Wednesday. Sterling was at $1.6080 in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  One trader at a Japanese city bank said the sharp pace of the dollar's fall against its Japanese counterpart could indicate a possible dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  through other Asian banks. \par \par \uc2  'Singapore has really sold a lot of dollars,' he said, adding that 'perhaps the U.S. sold dollars for Japan' in the mid-Y124.00 level. \par \par \uc2  Other traders said it's highly unlikely that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Support for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is pegged at Y123.75 yen, where Japanese life insurers are interested in buying. If the dollar falls through this level, next support is seen at Y123.45, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is seen trading between Y123.75-Y124.50 and DM1.6960-DM1.7020 for the rest of the Asian trading day. \par \par \uc2  Coinciding with the dollar's drop against the yen was a sharp fall in the dollar against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  Around 0058 GMT, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell sharply to HK$7.7450, compared with HK$7.7495 earlier in the session, on market talk that two of Hong Kong's largest banks are selling dollars to support the territory's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  following Deng Xiaoping's death Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is currently quoted at HK$7.7460 at 0117 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Traders said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in Japan aren't reacting significantly to the news of Deng's death. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 20-02-97 \par \par \uc2  0134GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt2k016js\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
