\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup: Dlr Up; Mkt Shrugs Off Local News Rpt \b0\par\par\uc2  By John Brinsley \par \uc2 329 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 1997\par 07:04\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (AP-Dow Jones)--A late report Monday from a local news wire saying that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its own if the dollar got too strong against the yen triggered some knee-jerk dollar selling that ended quickly. \par \par \uc2  The news wire reported that the U.S. and Japan made an agreement on this at the recent Group of Seven industrial nations meeting. \par \par \uc2  Otherwise, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets kept the dollar trading in a narrow range for much of Asian trading, wary of testing the prospect of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of key resistance around 125 yen and 1.7000 Deutsche marks. Nevertheless, the dollar is higher than its levels late Friday in New York. \par \par \uc2  The unconfirmed report that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  agreed to unilaterally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to halt any untoward dollar rise triggered some yen-buying, 'because there wasn't anything else to do,' said a Japanese bank trader. \par \par \uc2  'But a report saying \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  agrees to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  alone just means that it can't really do all that much to halt the dollar's rise,' he said. 'If the report had said the U.S. and Japan agree to stop the dollar, that would have meant more (dollar) selling.' \par \par \uc2  As a result, the dollar, which fell to intraday lows of Y124.15 and DM1.6897, soon came back on short-covering, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0545 GMT (12:45 a.m. EST), the dollar is quoted at Y124.43, above Y124.33 late Friday in New York and up from Y124.11 late Friday in London. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also is at DM1.6928, higher than DM1.6875 late Friday in New York and above DM1.6857 in London Friday. \par \par \uc2  The mark is quoted at Y73.51, down from Y73.68 in New York late Friday and below Y73.63 in London late Friday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-02-97 \par \par \uc2  0604GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt2h00ya4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
