\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo:Dlr Up But Top-Heavy On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fears \b0\par\par\uc2 270 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Februar 1997\par 01:49\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (AP-Dow Jones)--Buying by Tokyo interbanks has pushed up the dollar versus the yen, but continued fears of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is making the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  top-heavy. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is also higher versus the Deutsche mark in early Tokyo trading Friday compared with its levels late in New York Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Market talk that the Bank of England \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the BOJ to buy yen for dollars caused a flurry of dollar-selling by Japanese bank players late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  But most market players don't believe the U.K. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  actually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the dollar was bought back by Tokyo interbank players, traders said. \par \par \uc2  'There wasn't really (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), but Japanese banks sold' dollars, said a German bank dealer in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Unless fresh dollar-supportive factors emerge, market players see \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears preventing the dollar's rise to Y125.00 during Asian hours. \par \par \uc2  '\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rumors are making the dollar top-heavy, even though people want to buy dollars,' said a Japanese city bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Around 0047 GMT, the dollar is trading at Y124.48, down from Y124.50 around 0001 GMT but above Y124.40 yen in New York late Thursday. The dollar was quoted at Y124.20 yen late in Tokyo Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also trading at 1.6850 Deutsche marks, higher than DM1.6842 around 0001 GMT and just above DM1.6848 late Thursday in New York. The dollar was at DM1.6808 in Tokyo late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 14-02-97 \par \par \uc2  0049GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt2e0152u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
