\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  jitters grow as dlr nears 125 yen. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Donna Sells \par \uc2 305 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Feb 13 (Reuter) - With stampeding bulls continuing to push the dollar towards the key 125 yen barrier, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  experts noted mounting concern that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the rally, particularly when Tokyo trading gets underway. \par \par \uc2  "Everybody fears about BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  around 125 the figure," said Takayuki Ishikawa, assistant vice president at Tokai Bank Ltd. "But especially in New York time, I don't think they can do \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  Ishikawa added that he could see the dollar hitting 125 yen in the Tokyo market on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The greenback surged briefly to 124.66 yen in U.S. trade on Thursday, its highest level since the Group of Seven (G7) major powers last Saturday issued a statement declaring that "major misalignments" in exchange markets cited in its April 1995 communique have been corrected. \par \par \uc2  The dollar had tumbled to a post-World War II low of 79.75 yen on April 19, 1995. \par \par \uc2  Both the G7 and later Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  vowed to monitor \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and take appropriate actions. \par \par \uc2  "The central banks and governments seem to have set themselves up in a situation where, to save face, they are going to have to make some kind of material effort to cap the dollar," said Ron Leven, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at J.P. Morgan. \par \par \uc2  Leven said the BOJ is more likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  during Tokyo trading than in New York time. \par \par \uc2  If the dollar went above 125 yen in New York and the BOJ did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the market would not perceive a lack of concern at the BOJ, Leven said. \par \par \uc2  However, he said, "If we trade in Tokyo above 125 and we don't see them, then that's a more significant signal." \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dt2d00cp9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
