\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr/G-7 Statement -3: Threat Of Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Japan Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 266 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Februar 1997\par 23:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  At a minimum, the news from the G-7 meeting will continue to damp the dollar early next week, analysts forecast. The threat of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will also rein in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  'The markets may interpret this weekend's comments that in event of further yen weakness there will probably be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so the market should kick off fairly warily Monday,' said Neil MacKinnon, chief global strategist at Citibank in London. \par \par \uc2  At Saturday's meeting, Japan said the G-7 statement means the yen's strength against the dollar has been fully corrected, although the G-7 didn't specifically single out any \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  'Japan interprets the agreement to state that a correction in the strong yen has been achieved completely since April 1995,' Eisuke Sakakibara, director-general of the international finance bureau of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, economists said economic fundamentals are likely to be the most supportive factor for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Thomas Mayer, senior economist at Goldman Sachs in Frankfurt said, 'Even the nicest words can't change the facts that the Fed is going to raise interest rates eventually and that pressure is rising on the (Deutsche) Bundesbank to cut in the next months.' \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere Monday, market participants will also be eying the regular monthly meeting of G-10 central bankers at the Bank for International Settlements in Basel Monday for rejoinders to Saturday's G-7 remarks. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 08-02-97 \par \par \uc2  2227GMT \par \par \uc2  1149 4212 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt2800v36\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
