\par\par \b \uc2  =Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Watch -2:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Needs Policy Shift \b0\par\par\uc2 351 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 1997\par 06:20\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par And the BOJ may have sold dollars last Friday, though\par opinions are divided as to whether the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in fact\par entered the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to support the yen.\par    "The BOJ seems to tolerate the yen's weakness to some\par extent," says Tamotsu Yasuda, manager in the treasury &\par investment division at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi. "What the\par BOJ wants to avoid is a steep change in exchange rates. As\par long as the yen's weakening trend proceeds over a long\par period of time, the BOJ won't be concerned about levels."\par    Another concern for the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par economists say, is that BOJ \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par market is unlikely to have a lasting impact unless it's\par backed by a policy change - a hike in Japanese interest\par rates that would narrow the rate differential with the U.S.\par and thus counter one of the major factors behind the\par dollar's recent climb.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    But the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can't hike rates until the economy\par starts to show more consistent signs of recovery - and that\par isn't likely until at least the second half of 1997.\par    Before that, the economy has to weather the effects of a\par planned consumption tax hike and contractionary public\par spending in the new fiscal year beginning April 1.\par    "This has almost guaranteed the market that BOJ\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market now - not backed by a\par monetary policy change - will be ineffective," says\par Tetsufumi Yamakawa, senior economist at Goldman Sachs\par (Japan) Ltd. "The BOJ must be aware of this and wants to\par delay the timing of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," he adds.\par    Even so, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market remains highly\par sensitive in the short-term to suggestions the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par might \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to strengthen the yen.\par    The dollar fell Thursday on a comment Thursday by Eisuke\par Sakakibara, director at the Finance Ministry's International\par Finance Bureau, who was quoted in a local news report as\par saying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market\par when the timing is "effective."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) DOW JONES NEWS 01-31-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0020EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1138 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dt1v008lc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
