\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -2: U.S. Bond Rally On 4Q GDP Helps Dollar \b0\par\par\uc2 289 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 1997\par 23:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Wariness of taking the dollar too much higher is exactly why the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to break key resistance at DM1.6420, a level it tried to get to four times during Friday's global session, said Brian D. McCarthy, market analyst at Reusch International. \par \par \uc2  'There's a change in sentiment on the dollar - the market's a lot more negative - but there's still an appetite for dollars,' said a senior trader at a European bank in New York. 'The DM1.6300 level held, which means there's probably still some buyers out there that missed the rally.' \par \par \uc2  And the dollar's rally, in which it gained more than seven yen and 11 pfennigs since the start of the year, is exactly what many traders fear G-7 officials will tackle, either physically or verbally. \par \par \uc2  'Whatever they say, even if they say it as bland and vanilla as they can, will get a reaction from the market,' said Signet's Dix. \par \par \uc2  Already \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets are edgy that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its own to buoy the yen, a belief supported by recent remarks by Eisuke Sakakibara, the influential member of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  An MOF official has since said that Eisuke Sakakibara 'strongly denies' making such comments. \par \par \uc2  Strong fourth-quarter growth in the U.S., with the added bonus of subdued inflation, spurred a rally in U.S. bonds, helping the dollar recover some of its losses. \par \par \uc2  The economy clipped along at a 4.7% pace in the fourth quarter, faster than the 3.9% growth most economists expected. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 31-01-97 \par \par \uc2  2210GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 1865 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt1v00upn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
