\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup: Dollar Falls On Sakakibara Report \b0\par\par\uc2  By John Brinsley \par \uc2 295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Januar 1997\par 06:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (AP-Dow Jones)--A comment by a senior Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official reminding the market that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the yen remains an option started a wave of dollar selling, bringing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower Thursday from its levels in New York late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  A local news report quoting Eisuke Sakakibara, who heads MOF's International Finance Bureau, as saying \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market when the timing is effective, sent traders scrambling to unwind long dollar postions. \par \par \uc2  The comments underscored the speed of the dollar's rise against the yen so far this year, and the market took the opportunity to take profits, traders said. \par \par \uc2  But the short-term outlook for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains unchanged with most traders sceptical that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen. \par \par \uc2  'The market isn't really worried about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' said Makoto Kojima, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Barclays Bank in Tokyo. 'But most (market participants) are saying this level for the dollar is too fast.' \par \par \uc2  Others agreed, pointing out that the dollar strengthened about 12 yen last year, but has risen more than seven yen in January alone. \par \par \uc2  'The market is likely to take a bit of a rest,' said a trader at a Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  Around 0530 GMT (12:30 a.m. EST), the dollar is quoted at Y121.53, below Y122.05 late Wednesday in New York and down from Y121.99 yen late Wednesday in London. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also is at DM1.6408, lower than DM1.6434 late Wednesday in New York and below DM1.6428 marks in London Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 30-01-97 \par \par \uc2  0536GMT \par \par \uc2  1034 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt1u00nkv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
