\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -3: DEM Bought As EMU Concerns Arise \b0\par\par\uc2 303 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 1997\par 23:35\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Despite the dollar's surge, market players are convinced that the chance of actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets - by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  alone or in concert with others - is unlikely. \par \par \uc2  '\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is just futile and it lasts for only a short while,' said John Schein, vice president, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Generale Bank in New York. \par \par \uc2  In Tokyo, Mitsuzuka repeated that excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility is 'undesirable' and that the government would take steps should the need arise. \par \par \uc2  'I will only say that we will continue to monitor the market closely. This is the most effective way to achieve the stable market that we want,' he said at a news conference. \par \par \uc2  Also, Bank of Japan Governor Yasuo Matsushita said the country's monetary policy will be aimed at self-sustaining 'economic growth without inflation.' \par \par \uc2  'It's probably cheaper to talk ... than \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market,' said First Chicago's Ortiz. 'It's O.K. for the dollar to be stronger, they just don't want it at Y200 by next week. Their comments are an effort to slow it down.' \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, concerns arose once again over the prospects of Europe's monetary union after Germany, in its annual economic report, estimated that its 1997 deficit as a percentage of gross domestic product would be 2.9% - very close to the 3% limit set by the Maastricht Treaty. \par \par \uc2  Traders scooped up the mark in a safe-haven play, pushing it higher against other European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Portugal even \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , selling marks for escudos to stem the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall. \par \par \uc2  Reimut Jochimsen, a member of the Bundesbank's policy-making council, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was 'uncomfortable' with the government's forecast. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 29-01-97 \par \par \uc2  2235GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 1865 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt1t00n9s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
