\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ Sold/Traders -2: No Comment From BOJ \b0\par\par\uc2 164 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Januar 1997\par 09:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (AP-Dow Jones)--The Bank of Japan (BOJ) sold dollars for yen around Y120 late Friday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Opinions were divided on whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  actually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the talk swept through the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, sending the dollar from Y120 to below Y119.00. \par \par \uc2  'It certainly looks as if the BOJ was in,' said a trader at a Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  Japan's national television NHK reported in its 0800 GMT news broadcast that 'the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  went ahead with market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by buying the yen (for dollars) for the first time in four and a half years.' \par \par \uc2  The news report itself contributed to the dollar sell-off, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is seen having initial support around the mid Y118-level. \par \par \uc2  A BOJ spokesman didn't comment. \par \par \uc2  Around 0844 GMT, the dollar is at 118.83, down from its intraday high of Y120.13. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 24-01-97 \par \par \uc2  0848GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt1o00mmb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
