\par\par \b \uc2  Central Banks Not Seen Moving On  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Trends, For Now \b0\par\par\uc2  By Rebecca H. Patterson and Andrew Atkinson \par \uc2 264 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Januar 1997\par 14:09\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  LONDON (AP-Dow Jones)--Despite the dramatic and volatile start \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets have seen in 1997, don't look for major central banks to try and turn \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trends around - yet. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials and market insiders said Friday that concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  probably can't successfully reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements that have been set in place largely by economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  They think central banks will stay out of the game or limit \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to small 'smoothing' measures unless the dollar either starts to rise with substantially more momentum or reverses its recent gains completely, threatening economic recoveries in Europe and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  'We have always said in the past that if \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  goes against a general trend of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , (it is) useless,' a Deutsche Bundesbank spokesman told AP-Dow Jones News Services Friday. 'The only thing they can do is dampen erratic spurts, but they can't change a direction which is based on fundamentals. There is no change in our position.' \par \par \uc2  The Bundesbank's comments came hours after the Bank of Japan was reported to have entered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets during Asian trading Friday to stop the dollar's climb against the yen. \par \par \uc2  Shortly after the dollar hit a new 47-month high at Y120.13, news of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - later discounted by most market-watchers - brought the dollar down to just above Y118.50. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  wouldn't comment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  reports. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 24-01-97 \par \par \uc2  1309GMT \par \par \uc2  1192 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt1o00gl7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
