\par\par \b \uc2  Tokyo Midday: Dlr Up; Hits New 47-Mo High At Y119.33 \b0\par\par\uc2 330 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 1997\par 03:21\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (AP-Dow Jones)--After hitting a new 47-month high against the yen in morning trading Thursday, the dollar came off some on profit-taking, but is still higher than its levels earlier in the session. The dollar is up against the Deutsche mark as well. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose as high as Y119.33 around 0057 GMT, as stop-loss buying was triggered around Y119.20 and as interbank players bought the dollar. Short-term speculators including U.S. hedge funds sold the dollar, but it could still breach its earlier high, traders said. \par \par \uc2  'The dollar's trend is still up,' said a Japanese bank trader, who added that stop-loss buys are waiting if the dollar gets as high as Y119.60. \par \par \uc2  The market remains wary of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ). Traders dismissed unconfirmed rumors that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was checking rates around Y119.30, calling those rumors 'pure position talk.' \par \par \uc2  Ahead of the Group of Seven (G-7) meeting of finance ministers and central bankers in Berlin Feb. 8, the BOJ isn't likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  given dollar-supportive comments from U.S. and German officials, traders said. \par \par \uc2  'It's hard for the BOJ to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  right now,' said a trader at a Japanese commercial bank. 'They can't do it on their own, and no other G-7 (Group of Seven) country will support them.' \par \par \uc2  Around 0215 GMT, the dollar is at Y119.18, up from Y118.90 around 0025 GMT and above Y119.02 in New York late Wednesday. The dollar was at Y118.15 in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also trading at DM1.6401, higher than DM1.6380 earlier in Tokyo but below DM1.6418 late Wednesday in New York. The dollar was at DM1.6327 in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 23-01-97 \par \par \uc2  0221GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt1n00mjk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
