\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -2: Dollar Fell On Japan Mitsuzuka's Remarks \b0\par\par\uc2 343 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 1997\par 23:23\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  In his testimony,  Greenspan asked whether modest wage gains are 'transitional rather than a lasting phenomenon.' \par \par \uc2  Greenspan's speech had a 'tightening bias to it,' said Tim Stewart, global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Morgan Stanley in New York. 'It doesn't tip you over the edge on what (the Fed) might do Feb. 5, but ... there'll be a tightening in the first quarter.' \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Federal Open Market Committee holds its first policy-setting meeting of the year Feb. 4 and 5. \par \par \uc2  Rate increase or not, the global hunt for higher yields will continue to push the dollar up, Stewart said. 'The things that could dampen it are trade figures and signals from the (Group of 3 largest industrialized nations). Both those factors have been played down, not up. We've broken all sorts of technical levels, which is very positive for the dollar.' \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Barring any major hiccups, the dollar could test highs\par of   DM1.7000 and Y125 in the next few months, he added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The other excitement in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets came from Tokyo where\par Japanese Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka's assertion that the 'yen's\par weakness has gone too far' caused the dollar to tumble almost half a\par yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Mitsuzuka's remarks were later reversed, in part, by New York Fed\par President William McDonough's reiteration of U.S. Treasury Secretary\par Robert Rubin's strong dollar policy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The two met in Tokyo although they didn't discuss \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par rates, a Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Mitsuzuka's comments were followed by a flurry of remarks by Japanese\par government officials, including Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto,\par insisting the yen isn't too weak.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par One official, speaking on condition of anonymity, noted that Bank of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was powerless to alter the trend in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets.\par Volume in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market is 'far too big for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par to change the market's direction over the long term,' he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 21-01-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2223GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1033 1865 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt1l00fjj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
