\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -2: Markets Nervous  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Could  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Januar 1997\par 23:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  With the dollar now below 1.5900 marks 'the camp's divided, Duffy said. Some believe the decline provides an opportunity to buy at cheaper levels, while others believe the dollar has reached the peak of its current rally. \par \par \uc2  Some market players argue that growing confidence in a strong U.S. economy will continue to fuel the dollar's strength - much as in sterling where a bustling U.K. economy continues to attract buyers despite severe bouts of profit-taking. \par \par \uc2  The dollar could even shoot up to 120 yen, but at those levels and every point in between, 'everybody's anxious to take profits,' said Jeffrey Yu, vice president, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , at Sanwa Bank in New York. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, with the dollar consistently breaking key psychological barriers, market players are becoming jittery that central banks could make some noise - either talking the dollar lower or actually selling it. \par \par \uc2  'Everybody's watching whether the Bank of Japan or the (\b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) will do anything tonight,' said Sanway's Yu. 'The only viable thing for them is to say a weaker yen is not desirable. If they do sell dollars, they're taking a calculated risk of seeing the dollar fall 5 to 6 yen' and Japanese stocks sink. \par \par \uc2  'There could be some verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , because there's the danger that if the yen spirals down further, it could drag the Nikkei (stock index) down and Japan doesn't want that,' said Earl I. Johnson, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Bank of Montreal in Chicago. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, a lengthy monetary meeting in the U.K. yielded no clues as to where rates will move next. The results of the meeting, between the Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke and Bank of England Governor Eddie George, won't be known until Thursday. However, sterling trekked higher, fueled by a strong December U.K. jobs report. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 15-01-97 \par \par \uc2  2212GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt1f00ac6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
