\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -2: GBP Stormy As U.K. Rate-Rise Case Weakens \b0\par\par\uc2 319 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 1997\par 23:04\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The dollar's recent train of 45-month and 28-month highs against the yen and mark, respectively, has raised concerns in the market that central banks from Europe, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  - and even the U.S. - could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb excess price volatility. \par \par \uc2  However, at the Group-of-10 \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors meeting in Basel on Monday, the Bundesbank's Tietmeyer said there is no cause for concern over current exchange rate levels between the dollar and European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  or the rates among European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  themselves. Tietmeyer is also the chairman of the G-10 group. \par \par \uc2  Later, Tietmeyer said that central banks can't 'steer the exchange rate against the assessment of the markets.' He was speaking in Germany at the Walter Eucken Institute. \par \par \uc2  Tietmeyer's statements 'stopped the mark from restrengthening; he could have made comments positive for the mark' which would have weakened the dollar, said Graham Broyd, senior vice president of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at NatWest Markets. 'All the central bankers - the U.S., Germany, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  - have come to realize \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a very limited tool at best. Fiscal and monetary policies are much better ones.' \par \par \uc2  Also, U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin repeated the 'strong' dollar policy, noting its impact on keeping interest rates low and fostering other economic benefits. \par \par \uc2  Trading in sterling grew increasingly volatile as the case for an interest rate increase in Britain weakened. \par \par \uc2  Sterling received a beating Monday after U.K. producer input prices dropped a seasonally adjusted 0.5% in December from November while output prices rose only an unadjusted 0.5% - smaller than the forecast 0.7% increase. \par \par \uc2  Late in New York, sterling was at 2.6610 marks, down from 2.6677 marks. The British \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at 195.14 yen, down from 195.19 yen. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-01-97 \par \par \uc2  2204GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 1865 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt1d006iz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
