\par\par \b \uc2  Japan MOF Remarks Send Dlr Below 115 Yen; It's Up Again \b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 1997\par 04:33\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (AP-Dow Jones)--Japanese finance officials' remarks expressing concern over a 'excessively weak' yen helped trigger stop-loss dollar selling midday in Tokyo, sending the dollar below 115.00 yen before bargain hunters came in to buy the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back above that level. \par \par \uc2  Selling by U.S. hedge funds led the dollar down to an intraday low of 114.92 yen around 0245 GMT, and further sell orders were triggered as the dollar went through 115.50 yen and again at 115.20 yen, traders said. \par \par \uc2  'U.S. hedge funds were selling out of Singapore,' said Shuichi Noji, a dealer at Hokkaido Takushoku Bank. 'There were a few buy orders at 115.50 yen, but the (selling) momentum took the dollar through that level easily.' \par \par \uc2  However, Japanese importers bought the dollar around 115.00 yen, helping to reverse the trend and sending the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back up. \par \par \uc2  As reported, Hiroshi Mitsuzuka, head of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) said the ministry will respond to excessive yen moves and that excessive yen weakeness isn't desirable. \par \par \uc2  His remarks echoed comments by MOF administrative vice-minister Tadashi Ogawa Monday. \par \par \uc2  'Mituzuka's comments gave the market a good excuse to sell,' Noji said. \par \par \uc2  Vague market rumors about the possibility that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell dollars were greeted with scepticism. \par \par \uc2  'There's no reason for the BOJ to be in,' Noji said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0315 GMT, the dollar is at 115.16 yen, below 115.65 yen around 0210 GMT, and down from 115.76 yen in New York late Monday. The dollar was quoted at 116.61 yen in Tokyo late Monday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 07-01-97 \par \par \uc2  0333GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt1700300\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
