\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar finishes 1996 Tokyo up, but off day's high. \b0\par\par\uc2 526 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab      0630 GMT     2400 GMT\tab NYK CLOSE\par  USD/JPY\tab    115.95/05    115.70/73     115.25/35\par  USD/DEM\tab    1.5543/50    1.5528/33     1.5540/50\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Dec 30 (Reuter) - The dollar was standing at its highest level in 45 months in Tokyo against the yen on the last trading day of the year here, but failed to break above the high of 116.20 set in Friday's New York trade. \par \par \uc2  Carrying over the bullish sentiment from last week, and helped further by commercial buying, the dollar managed to rise as high as 116.18 yen before succumbing to profit-talking. \par \par \uc2  With participation limited ahead of the New Year holidays and no fresh incentives around, the dollar was merely moving along its recent bullish path, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The continued weakness in Japanese financial markets also gave dealers assurance in buying the dollar, they said. \par \par \uc2  The key Nikkei 225 stock index ended the final session of 1996 down 7.69 points or 0.04 percent at 19,361.35, after falling as low as 19,108.50. \par \par \uc2  But the greenback failed to climb above 116.20 yen as dealers were not inspired to try the topside and were content to take profits just below the New York high, they added. \par \par \uc2  "At this time of the year, why try anything new? Conventional wisdom tells you to take profits at the highs," said a dealer with a European bank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market closes for the year at 0900 GMT. Trade will resume on January 6. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers also said very small sales by exporters were detected at the highs, although other dealers said exporters had left sales orders placed at 116.30 and 116.50 yen prior to starting their holidays. \par \par \uc2  Movements in the dollar/mark arena were directionless, following in the footsteps of dollar/yen trade, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Some Singapore dealers said rumours of a European \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offering to sell at 1.5600 marks capped the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Most Tokyo dealers said they expect the dollar to head higher in the New Year, buoyed by a battered yen. \par \par \uc2  Weakness in Tokyo share prices has strengthened the view that Japan will be forced to keep its interest rates at record lows, leaving the yen less attractive than \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with higher yields such as the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Apart from frail stocks, a recent sell-off of yen bonds has aroused concerns of a "triple weakness", in which the yen is sold as capital flows out of Japanese stocks and bonds. \par \par \uc2  In addition, many participants do not expect monetary authorities to voice concern over the dollar's rise during the holiday period. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think authorities, especially those in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , will be able to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  even verbally ahead of the G7 meeting," said a trust bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The next meeting of finance ministers and central bankers of the Group of Seven (G7) nations is widely expeted to be held in late January or February. -- Jacqueline Wong, Singapore Newsroom (65 870 3088) -- George Nishiyama, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-5473-3710 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019dscu01t2n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
