\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  urged to reform  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2  system. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Yoshiko Mori \par \uc2 605 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 1996\par 05:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Dec 11 (Reuter) - Japanese monetary authorities are being urged to change the way they obtain financing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, and to follow other major G7 countries in making their \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  more transparent. \par \par \uc2  "It is urgent that the monetary authorities undertake a full review of the entire mechanism for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Sayuri Kawamura, a senior economist at \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Research Institute Ltd. \par \par \uc2  Japan has the world's largest external reserves at $217.11 billion, with much of that accumulated over the past several years through aggressive dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF), which decides when and at what amounts to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ), the agent for the \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , have been reluctant to release any information on their actions. \par \par \uc2  The central banks of other Group of Seven (G7) countries, such as the U.S. Federal Reserve and Germany's Bundesbank, disclose information in their quarterly and annual reports. \par \par \uc2  Taisuke Tanaka, market strategist at Credit Suisse Tokyo, said that although more openness might limit the effectiveness of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the public's right to know takes precedence. \par \par \uc2  "Preventing information from reaching the public may add to the effectiveness of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  because the market impact can be maximised through secrecy and unexpectedness." \par \par \uc2  "But, given the general direction in which people demand that the government be more accountable in its financial \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , MOF, too, is obliged to give an explanation of its actions," Tanaka said. \par \par \uc2  Kawamura said a review should involve public discussion on whether \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is cost-efficient and if such unlimited use of funds by the MOF for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is justifiable. \par \par \uc2  To foster debate, the monetary authorities must disclose more relevant data on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the actual sums used for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , she said. \par \par \uc2  MOF normally raises yen for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the issue of special \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  bills (FBs), which usually carry interest rates that are lower than prevailing market rates. \par \par \uc2  Due to the low yield, FBs are not always in great demand and the BOJ and other public entities are obligated to buy whatever issues are left unsold. Analysts say this financing method is at the core of the problem. \par \par \uc2  "It must be ideal for MOF to ensure a system that enables smooth access to funds at below market rates, particularly since \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy has high priority in Japan," Tanaka said. \par \par \uc2  However, the large amount of cash made readily available to MOF for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has led to the large accumulation of external reserves, which in turn has exposed the government to significant \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks, Tanaka added. \par \par \uc2  MOF data shows \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  losses from past \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  are expected to top 10 trillion yen ($88.4 billion) by the end of this fiscal year in March 1997. \par \par \uc2  However, current accounting methods do not require MOF to realise these massive \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  losses. \par \par \uc2  The issuing of FBs normally needs to be discussed and approved by parliament, but there is apparently no debate. \par \par \uc2  The financing mechanism for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has in reality led to the underwriting of government debt by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is banned under Japanese law, Kawamura said. \par \par \uc2  FB purchases are also hurting the BOJ's portfolio as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  must unload holdings of other short-term securities with attractive yields to buy them. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ has made no secret of its discontent over MOF's reliance on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to finance \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, an influential academic group has proposed to a panel advising Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto that the BOJ be banned from underwriting FBs. ($1=113 yen) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019dscb02bpg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
