\par\par \b \uc2  Fed's Greenspan -3: Japan Officials Strongly Support Reform \b0\par\par\uc2 287 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 1996\par 04:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Asked if he thought a 'big bang' deregulation of financial markets would boost the internationalization of the yen, Greenspan said 'I don't see how it can fail.' \par \par \uc2  But he emphasized that internationalization of the yen wouldn't come at the expense of the dollar or the Euro. \par \par \uc2  As for governments setting target ranges for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates, Greenspan said he hasn't seen any evidence that such measures work. He said the 'the burden of proof' should be on anyone who advocates target ranges. \par \par \uc2  Greenspan said that whether \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy is the responsibility of the finance ministry or \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't matter, as either system works. \par \par \uc2  He noted that the Fed 'works with the U.S. Treasury to make judgments about the degree of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  Greenspan said his understanding is that there won't be much change in the way Japan conducts \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. Japan's Finance Ministry has ultimate responsibility for setting \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, but works with the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  Greenspan has been in Tokyo since Sunday at the invitation of Bank of Japan Governor Yasuo Matsushita. In addition to talks with Matsushita, Greenspan met Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka and Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto. \par \par \uc2  Greenspan praised Hashimoto's recent announcement to aggressively deregulate Japan's financial markets and a report by a government panel calling for the Bank of Japan to become more independent. Greenspan said he 'suspects' financial reform will 'succeed' and that the degree of commitment by Japanese government officials to implement reform was higher than he expected. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 19-11-96 \par \par \uc2  0313GMT \par \par \uc2  4205 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011014dsbj013o6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
