\par\par \b \uc2  Japan BOJ Matsushita-4:To Cooperate With Govt On Fin Crisis \b0\par\par\uc2 169 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 November 1996\par 12:07\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  On the Bank of Japan's role in international \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Matsushita said currently he doesn't see the need for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to have authority over \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  currently does the actual \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as the Finance Ministry's agent, and the government has the responsibility to conduct \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy that has direct impact to the market, Matsushita noted. \par \par \uc2  The panel's proposals made clear that as long as the Bank of Japan respects that role of the government, it has freedom to conduct international \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Matsushita said. \par \par \uc2  On a lack of specific guidelines for Bank of Japan loans in cases of liquidity crunch, and an apparent leadership of the government in dealing with financial system crisis, Matsushita said the Bank of Japan will continue to cooperate with the government in providing necessary liquidity to restore financial system stability. \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES NEWS 11-12-96 \par \par \uc2  0607EST \par \par \uc2  4077 4210 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011013dsbc02pfu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
