\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  govt should not  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  - MOF. \b0\par\par\uc2 459 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 November 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Nov 8 (Reuter) - The Japanese government should not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, newly appointed Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka told Reuters on Friday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets move in line with trends in global trade and the world's market economy, he said. \par \par \uc2  "Markets are by nature things that move, and all I can say is that we will keep careful watch. It's not something that we should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in," Mitsuzuka said, without elaborating. \par \par \uc2  "The market will naturally reflect the strength of Japan's economy, and I am not very worried (about the current state of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market)," he said. \par \par \uc2  "The market is moving in a way that reflects (Japan's) overall economic conditions," Mitsuzuka said. \par \par \uc2  In order to put the economy on a stable growth trend, it is important to steadily implement fiscal and monetary policies such as fiscal reforms and flexibility in formulating a state budget, he said. \par \par \uc2  Mitsuzuka said there was no doubt that Japan's economy was on a gradual recovery trend, but not all industries were on a recovery trend as was shown in various surveys. \par \par \uc2  Regarding the fact that the Bank of Japan (BOJ) has kept the official discount rate at a record low of 0.5 percent for more than a year, he said the primary and secondary industries as well as small firms were happy with this situation. \par \par \uc2  Asked whether the BOJ was likely to maintain the current policy of keeping interest rates low, Mitsuzuka said: "Yes, I think this will continue." \par \par \uc2  Asked whether such a policy was needed to help the economy, he said: "I think we do need it, at the moment." \par \par \uc2  Regarding a supplementary budget for fiscal 1996/97 ending March, he said the government would draft a budget to cover the necessary costs for areas such as those for the reconstruction of Kobe after the earthquake there in January 1995, and for funds to help the growth of new technologies centreing on information and communications. \par \par \uc2  However, the government cannot follow the precedent of heaping money on public works, Mitsuzuka said when asked whether stimulative measures should be included in the extra budget. \par \par \uc2  Regarding the revision of laws to boost the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's independence, Mitsuzuka said he would like to see the government submit bills to the next regular session of parliament starting in January and make them into law. \par \par \uc2  He said he would respect a report to be submitted by a governmental study group on the issue, and make any additions to it if needed, as the issue also concerns his ministry. \par \par \uc2  The study group is expected to submit the report to the prime minister by the end of this year. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018dsb800p8c\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (japan near10 interve